<title>USA: Duff &amp; Phelps to downgrade AT&amp;T Capital.</title>
<headline>Duff &amp; Phelps to downgrade AT&amp;T Capital.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Duff &amp; Phelps Credit Rating Co said Tuesday it plans to downgrade the credit ratings of AT&amp;T Capital Corp, which is 80 percent owned by AT&amp;T Corp, following completion of the company's sale to a leasing consortium.</p>
<p>The downgrades will become effective on the date of the merger's closing, which is expected in early October.</p>
<p>The ratings affected include the senior long-term debt, from Single A to Triple B and commercial paper from D One to D Two.</p>
<p>-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
</text>
